{{link|https://www.m365.fm/categories/azure-talk/|Azure}} Cloud Adoption Framework strategy, business case, TCO modeling, FinOps and governance debt – {{link|https://www.m365.fm/the-azure-caf-nobody-follows-but-should/|this episode}} is for people searching “Azure CAF strategy phase”, “cloud adoption business case CFO”, “Azure TCO calculator”, “landing zone governance debt”, “cloud economics for CFOs” or “how to align Azure strategy with workloads”. If your Azure “strategy” lives as buzzword bingo in SharePoint and nobody can connect it to real workloads or numbers, this conversation shows how CAF Strategy and Plan actually break in the wild – and how to rebuild them so your CFO, architects and engineers finally read the same map.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68017163/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68017163/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}} We start where most journeys wobble: the Strategy stage nobody reads twice. On paper, CAF says you should document motivations and outcomes; in reality, strategy docs collapse into vague slogans like “future‑proofing” and “innovation at scale” that sound nice but don’t tell anyone which workloads to move, which Azure services to use or what success looks like. We walk through how that fluff creates “strategic drift”: landing zones designed without clear consumers, endless subscription and networking debates, and security baselines built on sand because nobody tied “be more agile” to specific SQL instances, apps or recovery objectives. You’ll hear how to flip those slogans into short, measurable commitments—naming workloads, services and metrics—so a CIO, finance analyst and tech lead can all point at the same target instead of arguing over interpretations.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68017163/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68017163/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}} From there, we move into the CAF Plan phase and the business case CFOs actually believe. Slides about “synergy” and pastel arrows repel finance; they want upfront cost, break‑even timelines and clear ownership if Azure spend explodes. We discuss how to use Azure Migrate assessments and the TCO calculator properly instead of guessing, how to model Reserved Instances, Savings Plans and Azure Hybrid Benefit in real numbers, and how to translate technical levers into business outcomes like avoided hardware refresh, reduced ticket volume or predictable three‑year spend. The result is a plan that doesn’t just promise “savings someday” but spells out next quarter’s cloud bill, when it pays back, and who takes responsibility if it doesn’t.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68017163/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68017163/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}} Finally, we tackle the forgotten strategy that dies in SharePoint and turns into governance debt. Even solid CAF Strategy and Plan outputs often get archived and ignored while teams chase landing zones, tags and resource groups—useful work, but disconnected from the original outcomes and financial assumptions. We talk about how to keep strategy “alive” with living documents, review cadences and simple checkpoints that tie back every big decision (like new regions, SKUs or patterns) to the original motivations and workloads. You’ll hear how to surface cost and governance drift early, use CAF tools as recurring guardrails instead of one‑off templates, and avoid waking up three years later with a cloud estate that technically “runs” but no longer matches the business case anyone signed off. WHAT YOU WILL LEARN
- Why most Azure CAF strategies fail by staying vague and workload‑free.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68017163/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68017163/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How to rewrite buzzword‑heavy strategy into short, measurable, workload‑anchored commitments.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68017163/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68017163/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How the CAF Plan phase can either win or lose your CFO in a single meeting.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68017163/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68017163/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How to use Azure Migrate and the TCO calculator to build a defensible cost model.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68017163/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68017163/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How Reserved Instances, Savings Plans and Hybrid Benefit change the financial story.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68017163/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68017163/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- Why ignoring strategy after kickoff creates governance and cost “debt” downstream.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68017163/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68017163/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How to keep CAF artifacts alive with reviews, owners and decision checkpoints.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68017163/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68017163/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- A practical pattern for aligning cloud strategy, workloads and cloud economics so finance, IT and business stay on the same page.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68017163/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68017163/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}

THE CORE INSIGHT The core insight of this episode is that Azure CAF doesn’t fail because Microsoft’s framework is broken—it fails when Strategy and Plan stay fluffy, get filed away and never shape real workloads or numbers. Once you attach clear outcomes to named workloads, show CFO‑grade cost models and keep those decisions alive throughout adoption and governance, CAF turns from a pretty poster into a working playbook your architects, admins and finance team can actually follow. {{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68017163/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68017163/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}WHO THIS IS FOR
- Cloud architects and platform owners using or considering the Azure Cloud Adoption Framework.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68017163/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68017163/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- CIOs and IT leaders struggling to link Azure work to business outcomes and budgets.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68017163/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68017163/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- CFOs, FinOps and finance partners who want real numbers, not cloud buzzwords.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68017163/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68017163/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- Cloud governance and landing zone teams tired of strategy that never shows up in designs.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68017163/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68017163/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- Anyone who has watched an Azure “strategy deck” vanish into SharePoint while costs and complexity kept rising.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68017163/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68017163/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}

ABOUT THE HOST Mirko Peters is a Microsoft 365 consultant and host of M365.FM, where he explores modern work, security and productivity with Microsoft 365 and Azure. He helps organizations turn Azure CAF from a checkbox exercise into a grounded strategy and plan, connecting workloads, cloud economics and governance so both tech and finance leaders know exactly why they’re in the cloud and how they’ll measure success. Become a supporter of this podcast: {{link|https://www.spreaker.com/podcast/m365-fm-microsoft-365-azure-cloud-power-platform-ai--6704921/support?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=rss|https://www.spreaker.com/podcast/m365-fm-microsoft-365-azure-cloud-power-platform-ai--6704921/support}}.

